# Without this file, line endings for every text file depend entirely on
# each contributor's local `core.autocrlf` setting -- Windows Git's common
# default (core.autocrlf=true) checks these out as CRLF. That's invisible
# for most editing, but broke __tests__/full-menu-scroll-refresh-safety.test.ts
# outright: it reads components/FullMenuScroll.tsx as a raw string and
# looks for exact substrings containing a literal "\n", which a CRLF file
# never matches (confirmed by reproducing a CRLF checkout locally -- it
# fails all 4 of that file's marker-dependent tests). Forcing LF here makes
# every checkout byte-identical regardless of OS or git config, which is
# what that test (and any future one doing the same kind of raw source-text
# matching) actually needs to be reliable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets -- never text-convert these regardless of extension.
*.mp4 binary
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
